# Machine-local access policy

Configure and save this file as `ACCESS_POLICY.md` on each server before using
an agent. Replace every placeholder; do not inherit another server's paths.

## Allowed reads

- This repository checkout: `<ABSOLUTE_PROJECT_ROOT>`.
- Dataset roots explicitly authorized on this server: `<DATASET_ROOTS>`.
- Model/cache roots explicitly authorized here: `<MODEL_CACHE_ROOTS>`.

## Allowed writes

- This repository checkout, including `.git`, shared source/documentation,
  `.venv`, and local `outputs`, `runs`, `state` and `workspace` artifacts.
- Only explicitly authorized external dataset/cache destinations:
  `<WRITABLE_EXTERNAL_ROOTS_OR_NONE>`.

Everything else is denied by default. Do not inspect other users' files,
credentials, SSH keys, shell history or unrelated repositories. Normal Git
transport may use the user's configured authentication; never copy credentials
into this project. Follow the server's compute and dataset-download policy.

## Dataset lookup

Before downloading, inspect the active plan, any project dataset link whose
resolved target is allowed, then the authorized dataset roots. Record findings
in `workspace/dataset_inventory.md`. Download one missing dataset at a time to
an explicitly writable dataset-specific destination. Do not upload datasets,
model weights or caches to Git.
